# Python Standards

Source: [python.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) — Flask sections removed

## Style
- PEP 8: `snake_case` functions/vars, `PascalCase` classes, `UPPER_SNAKE` constants
- Type hints on all public function signatures and return values
- Absolute imports from `src.*`; backend root on `PYTHONPATH` via pytest config
- Max line length 100 (match `ruff` in `pyproject.toml`)

## Typing
- Prefer `X | None` over `Optional[X]` (Python 3.11+)
- Use `Protocol` for repository interfaces and provider adapters
- Pydantic models for external boundaries; dataclasses for internal benchmark metrics

## Project layout
- Source in `backend/src/`; tests in `backend/tests/` mirroring module paths
- Config in `backend/configs/` YAML; secrets via environment variables only

## Testing
- pytest; async tests with `pytest-asyncio`
- `conftest.py` fixtures for sample events, campaigns, temp data dirs
- No live LLM calls in unit tests — mock `provider_registry` or use heuristic judge mode

## Documentation
- Google-style docstrings on public classes and non-obvious functions
- Module-level docstring for packages under `containment/`, `benchmark/`, `data/`
